127
00:23:47,334 --> 00:23:57,654
冷たい冬の風が もうすぐ埋める 吐息で凍らす歌
The cold winter wind will soon bury the song frozen by our sighs

128
00:23:58,794 --> 00:24:08,304
街はイルミネーション 魔法をかけたみたい 裸足の足が痛む 冬のきらめき
The town is illuminated, as if cast in magic; my barefoot feet ache in the winter sparkle

129
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:17,964
どうしても言えなかった この気持ち 抑え付けて泣けた
No matter what, I couldn't say it—I suppressed these feelings and cried

130
00:24:18,834 --> 00:24:24,904
前から決めていたことだから これでいいの すべて嘘じゃないから
It's something I decided long ago, so this is fine, because none of it was a lie

131
00:24:25,204 --> 00:24:30,334
すてきな想い出なんて 言えたなら きっと嘘つきだな
If I could call it a wonderful memory, then I'd surely be a liar

132
00:24:30,924 --> 00:24:40,504
ありがとう さようなら 切ない片想い 想い出したら想い出してしてしまうから
Thank you, goodbye, such a painful unrequited love... if I remember it, I'll just end up remembering too much

133
00:24:40,504 --> 00:24:45,944
ありがとう さようなら 寂しくないから寂しくないから
Thank you, goodbye, I'm not lonely, I'm not lonely...

134
00:24:46,594 --> 00:24:51,464
そう思った瞬間 ふわりと 舞い降りてくる雪 触れたら溶けて消えた
The moment I thought that, snow softly fluttered down, and when I touched it, it melted and vanished

135
00:25:07,004 --> 00:25:13,524
キミとあと続くおどり よりそってふたり楽しそう ほらみて初雪
Walking behind you in secret, the two of you snuggling close, looking so happy, look, it's the first snow.

136
00:25:17,794 --> 00:25:28,214
君とあんなふうに なりたくて初めて作った手編みのマフラー
Wanting to be like that with you, I made a hand-knitted scarf for the very first time.

137
00:25:29,094 --> 00:25:34,924
どうしたら私伝えられたんだろ 口なしのこわかっただけ
How should I have told you? I was just too chicken and scared.

138
00:25:35,894 --> 00:25:44,754
想い出になるなら このままでかまわないってそうごまかして 本当はなの
If it becomes just a memory, I said I didn't mind, but I was just kidding myself, really...

139
00:25:45,694 --> 00:25:55,154
ねえ 本当のありがとうさよなら いつかこんな時が来てしまうこと ここわかってたはずだわ
Saying a true "thank you" and "goodbye"—I must have known this moment would come someday.

140
00:25:59,794 --> 00:26:05,884
ねえ ありがとう さよなら からだがふるえてる
Hey, thank you, goodbye, my body is trembling.

141
00:26:06,794 --> 00:26:10,924
もうすぐ列車が来るのに
Even though the train will be arriving soon...

142
00:26:11,794 --> 00:26:19,214
それは今になって 私を苦しめる りがいたい
Now that's what hurts me... it aches so much.

143
00:26:20,794 --> 00:26:26,124
どれほど願いあっただろう
Just how much did we wish for this?

144
00:26:26,794 --> 00:26:36,214
この手を離したら ねえ さよならだって
If I let go of this hand... saying "goodbye"...

145
00:26:36,794 --> 00:26:51,794
こういうここ
Right here...

146
00:26:59,794 --> 00:27:09,214
できなくちゃ そんなのはわかる 君が優しいことも知ってる
We can't do that, I know. I also know how kind you are.

147
00:27:09,794 --> 00:27:20,214
だから この手をはなしてよ 出会えてよかった 君が好き
So let go of this hand. I'm glad I met you, I love you.

148
00:27:20,794 --> 00:27:34,214
ありがとうさよなら 一言が言えない 今だけは私に勇気を
Thank you, goodbye—I can't even say a single word. Please give me courage, just for now.

149
00:27:36,794 --> 00:27:42,214
今だけは泣いていいよね
It's okay to cry right now, right?

150
00:27:42,794 --> 00:27:55,214
もう言葉はいらない 骨がぎゅっとしていて
I don't need any more words, just hold me tight.

151
00:28:04,794 --> 00:28:20,794
どんな私がいて どんな君がいるのか
What kind of me is here, and what kind of you is there...

152
00:28:28,504 --> 00:28:31,644
Whoa, you got some extensions?

153
00:28:32,724 --> 00:28:35,484
Extensions? I don't remember getting anything like that.

154
00:28:35,684 --> 00:28:38,244
Your hair is even longer!

155
00:28:38,424 --> 00:28:39,604
It's fashionable though, don't you think?

156
00:28:39,824 --> 00:28:41,364
It looks kind of familiar...

157
00:28:41,764 --> 00:28:43,684
Oh, like maybe we're missing some... Oh, that was...

158
00:28:43,844 --> 00:28:45,924
Oh, you have another arm too?

159
00:28:46,144 --> 00:28:50,004
Whoa there, hold on a second! Something's kind of strange. It's growing out!

160
00:28:50,184 --> 00:28:53,944
Not only has the season changed, but it looks like we've lost someone!

161
00:28:54,084 --> 00:28:56,344
Oh, come back! Hi! Hello!

162
00:28:56,904 --> 00:28:57,944
You're here! You're here!

163
00:28:58,304 --> 00:28:59,964
Ina! Nice, nice hair!

164
00:29:00,164 --> 00:29:03,804
The seasons have changed! Yes, it's getting a little warmer, thank goodness.

165
00:29:03,964 --> 00:29:10,784
It was kind of cool these past few... a little chilly, especially for me and Kiara's song. It's become spring!

166
00:29:10,984 --> 00:29:12,184
Wow, beautiful!

167
00:29:12,544 --> 00:29:14,464
Look at that, the stage is so pink!

168
00:29:14,624 --> 00:29:17,964
I actually really like the color pink now after these six years.

169
00:29:18,164 --> 00:29:20,244
Oh, character development!

170
00:29:20,564 --> 00:29:22,044
The seasons... That's good, that's good.

171
00:29:22,244 --> 00:29:23,604
Wow, princess!

172
00:29:23,764 --> 00:29:28,244
And we're wearing yukata, kimono, whatever you wanted it to be. And we all went for kind of a blue color, huh?

173
00:29:28,524 --> 00:29:31,504
Yeah, we do look like we're about to drop a sweet enka album.

174
00:29:32,004 --> 00:29:35,084
This isn't how they pose... dokkoisho dokkoisho!

175
00:29:36,704 --> 00:29:42,084
soran soran soran soran...

176
00:29:42,924 --> 00:29:48,164
Okay, that's not what we're doing when we're releasing though...

177
00:29:48,664 --> 00:29:50,544
So we did a bunch of songs, like...

178
00:29:50,864 --> 00:29:54,084
For example... September? That's not the one that you sang!

179
00:29:57,704 --> 00:30:02,984
No, please please, wait, this is a really iconic old Japanese song, okay? Did a lot of posing.

180
00:30:04,376 --> 00:30:08,376
Well, we have also changed costume.
Well, we have also changed costumes.

181
00:30:08,596 --> 00:30:09,196
Yes.

182
00:30:09,373 --> 00:30:13,033
We're so blue and pink, white blue pink, red white and blue...

183
00:30:13,033 --> 00:30:15,033
Wait, I'm blue.

184
00:30:15,233 --> 00:30:19,633
Not quite. Goldish kino, and... miserable, cause I lost purple pearls.

185
00:30:19,933 --> 00:30:22,633
Ah, soldane!
Ah, true!

186
00:30:22,933 --> 00:30:25,033
Wait, is this Morning Glory?

187
00:30:25,133 --> 00:30:26,533
Ah, I thought they were jellyfish.

188
00:30:26,733 --> 00:30:28,533
Are they jellyfish?

189
00:30:28,733 --> 00:30:32,533
No, I think it's morning glory.

190
00:30:32,533 --> 00:30:36,533
It could be, it could also be Austrian bread.

191
00:30:36,533 --> 00:30:39,233
Called Semmel.

192
00:30:39,433 --> 00:30:41,533
That's exactly the shape of Austrian bread.

193
00:30:41,733 --> 00:30:44,033
Do the breads come in those colors?

194
00:30:44,233 --> 00:30:46,633
No, only if they're moldy!

195
00:30:46,633 --> 00:30:51,033
Lala, hope you never eat one of those. Don't eat moldy bread!
Hahaha, hope you never eat one of those. Don't eat moldy bread!

196
00:30:51,033 --> 00:30:55,433
Yeah, we know you're... you're aware of that. Have you eaten moldy bread before, everybody?

197
00:30:55,433 --> 00:30:57,233
Are you sure?

198
00:30:57,433 --> 00:31:00,233
Probably stale... stale bread.

199
00:31:00,433 --> 00:31:02,433
Why is this what we're talking about during our concert?

200
00:31:02,633 --> 00:31:05,433
It's okay, a little whimsy is fine.

201
00:31:05,633 --> 00:31:09,833
But now how about we get serious for a moment and sing a kyokusetsu?

202
00:31:09,833 --> 00:31:12,633
Kyoku... let's sing a kyoku.

203
00:31:12,833 --> 00:31:17,233
Let's sing a song. Let's sing a song that's a little bit EMO.

204
00:31:17,233 --> 00:31:29,233
I was listening to the lyrics and practicing it, and I was like, "Hmm, you know, there are a couple lyrics here and there that remind me of like the struggles that we have gone through and how I want to go forward with you guys."

205
00:31:29,433 --> 00:31:33,433
So it made me kind of like, "Ah, emo," so I hope we can sing it well together.

206
00:31:33,433 --> 00:31:36,033
We will! We will!

207
00:31:36,233 --> 00:31:39,433
Let's do it in these slightly restrictive... but they're really stretchy outfits.

208
00:31:39,633 --> 00:31:41,433
Okay. All right, enough of that.

209
00:31:41,633 --> 00:31:45,433
Yeah, you like that. You like that, don't you? Close your eyes.

210
00:31:45,633 --> 00:31:48,933
All right, please shut your eyes, start to chill out, dance, and sing.

211
00:31:49,133 --> 00:31:51,433
All right, let's listen to our next song, Suzume.

212
00:34:34,082 --> 00:34:39,942
鎌平のなかでひらりあいたのは青き線
In Kamahira, fluttering open was a blue line

213
00:34:40,202 --> 00:34:45,782
それらが結ばれるのは真の空
What ties them together is the true sky

214
00:34:46,022 --> 00:34:54,142
風の中でも負けないような声で届けた言葉をいまは育ててる
With a voice that won't lose even in the wind, I am now nurturing the words I delivered

215
00:35:04,260 --> 00:35:09,240
わざとじゃない　人は影を
It's not on purpose... People cast shadows...

216
00:35:10,290 --> 00:35:15,340
なんて泣いてるの時かけ答えれる
Why are you crying? When did you learn to answer?

217
00:35:15,540 --> 00:35:20,940
涙なんかじゃ　僕ら出会ったことの意味にはまるんだ
Tears alone won't capture the meaning of the day we met...

218
00:35:21,440 --> 00:35:28,540
追いつかないこの身ひとつじゃ足りない叫び
This single body cannot catch up... A mere cry is not enough...

219
00:35:28,940 --> 00:35:33,940
君の手が触れた時にだけ震えた心があったよ
Only when your hand touched mine, did my heart tremble...

220
00:35:34,440 --> 00:35:40,640
君をいくつ超えれば僕らはたどり着けるのかな
How many of you must I cross to finally reach where we belong?

221
00:35:41,140 --> 00:35:46,640
見る草でいい　正しさのその先で君と手をつなぎたい
Any grass will do... Beyond what is right, I want to hold your hand...

222
00:36:05,940 --> 00:36:10,640
想い出せない　大切な記憶
I cannot remember... those precious memories...

223
00:36:10,940 --> 00:36:16,940
言葉にならない　ここにある想い
They won't turn into words... the feelings resting here...

224
00:36:18,140 --> 00:36:29,140
もしかなしたら　もしかなしたら　それだけでこの心はできてる
What if... what if that alone is what my heart is made of?

225
00:36:30,440 --> 00:36:35,640
もしかなしたら　もしかなしたら
What if... what if...

226
00:36:35,940 --> 00:36:44,940
君に気付いてと今のその胸を打ち鳴らす
I beat upon my chest, wanting you to notice me right now...

227
00:36:59,440 --> 00:37:04,940
なんて泣いてるの時かけ答えれる
Why are you crying? When did you learn to answer?

228
00:37:05,240 --> 00:37:10,440
涙なんかじゃ　僕ら出会ったことの意味にはまるんだ
Tears alone won't capture the meaning of the day we met...

229
